<title>FRANCE: GAN 1996 net loss 5.683 bln francs.</title>
<headline>GAN 1996 net loss 5.683 bln francs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable		loss     5,683  vs  loss   1,786</p>
<p>    Life assurance France			825  vs	     451</p>
<p>    Non-life insurance France   loss	 112  vs  loss     567</p>
<p>    Insurance international		    321  vs	     496</p>
<p>    Insurance total			    1,034  vs	     380</p>
<p>    Insurance exceptional items   charge 1,365  vs  gain     700</p>
<p>    CIC bank unit result	   700  vs	     732</p>
<p>    Other bank, finance units   loss	 752  vs  loss	96</p>
<p>    UIC property unit	     loss     7,985  vs  loss   1,849</p>
<p>    Defeasance structure		     2,685  vs  loss   1,653</p>
<p>    Total in property banking   loss     5,300  vs  loss   3,502</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said in February 27 it expected a 1996 loss of five billion francs. It said in a results statement the 2.685 billion positive result for the property defeasance structure took into account state financing guarantees.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
